<Base title="About" active="about" description="Learn about Nikhil Joglekar, a CIPP/E and CIPM-certified privacy and data protection professional."><section class="page-head container"><span class="kicker">THE PERSON BEHIND THE PERSPECTIVE</span><h1>Curiosity, clarity<br/>and <em>context.</em></h1><p>I’m a privacy and data protection professional who believes that understanding the purpose behind a rule matters just as much as knowing the rule itself.</p></section><div class="container page-rule"></div><section class="container about-body two-column"><div class="aside-label"><span class="kicker">01 / MY STORY</span><div class="mini-art" aria-hidden="true"><span>NJ.</span></div></div><div class="rich-copy"><h2>Hello, I'm Nikhil.</h2><p>My work focuses on data protection, privacy governance and the challenges organizations face as technology evolves. I’ve worked across international privacy matters spanning regulatory analysis, commercial arrangements and operational privacy considerations.</p><p>Over time, I’ve become especially interested in a question that connects many of these topics: how can organizations translate complex rules into decisions that are practical, accountable and built to last?</p><p>This site is where I explore that question through independent writing on data protection, AI governance and responsible technology.</p><div class="inline-credentials"><div><small>PROFESSIONAL CREDENTIALS</small><strong>CIPP/E · CIPM</strong></div><div><small>AREAS OF INTEREST</small><strong>Privacy · AI Governance · Digital Trust</strong></div></div></div></section><section class="soft-section"><div class="container two-column"><div><span class="kicker">02 / WHAT GUIDES MY THINKING</span><h2 class="sub-heading">Principles over<br/><em>posturing.</em></h2></div><div class="values-list"><div><span>01</span><div><h3>Clarity over complexity</h3><p>Making complicated ideas accessible without flattening the nuance that matters.</p></div></div><div><span>02</span><div><h3>Implementation over abstraction</h3><p>Connecting legal requirements to decisions, workflows and actual organizational practices.</p></div></div><div><span>03</span><div><h3>Thoughtfulness over certainty</h3><p>As law and technology change, the willingness to question assumptions becomes essential.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="container closing-cta"><span class="kicker">WHAT I'M EXPLORING</span><h2>Ideas worth <em>unpacking.</em></h2><p>My writing is an ongoing exploration rather than a claim to have all the answers.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="/insights">Browse insights <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section></Base>
